    thinking: "**Analyzing the Request**\n\nI\'m carefully dissecting this request, identifying the core elements: new section creation, positioning specifics (top-right, bottom-left), and a \"subscribe\" element with a title and design instructions. I\'m focusing on how these components interact and the specific constraints implied by \"all screen same.\"\n\n\n**Refining the Design**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the visual aspects, particularly the droplet patterns for the all-screen layout. My attention is on replicating the existing droplet styles from `DropletPattern.tsx` or similar components. I\'m visualizing the banner card: a dark container with rounded corners (potentially `rounded-3xl`), holding text content and a small tag. The objective is to ensure the droplet pattern\'s seamless consistency across devices.\n\n\n**Constructing the Newsletter Banner**\n\nI\'m currently building the newsletter banner. I\'m focusing on the \"Join our community\" subtitle using a clean sans-serif font with light text. The heading, \"Subscribe to our newsletter,\" will be bold white and centered, featuring a red/orange curved underline (like an arc/brush swoosh). Below, I\'m working on the paragraph text\342\200\224centered, grey/light, and a readable font size. The email input and subscribe button will have a pill-shaped design.\n\n\n"
